{
  "id": "R017Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Ultrasound",
  "description": "An ultrasound uses high-frequency sound waves to create real-time images of internal organs, tissues, and blood flow. This painless outpatient test requires no radiation and no needles. A technician applies gel to your skin and moves a small probe, instantly showing images on a screen. The procedure takes 15-45 minutes depending on what's being evaluated. Ultrasound safely evaluates pregnancy, organs, blood vessels, joints, and soft tissues. Results guide diagnosis and treatment planning. You go home immediately and can resume all activities. This type of procedure can be performed various ways, including prenatal, standard, and vascular / doppler duplex, and the cost may vary depending on the specific approach or service provided.",
